WEBVTT

00:00:00.608 --> 00:00:04.099
Caerina, that move was pretty impressive,

00:00:04.344 --> 00:00:09.102
but you'll need around this much oomph
to get rid of a rock golem.

00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:12.003
Weapon Skill: Zamzer Blade!

00:00:22.364 --> 00:00:24.826
Magic Skill: Zan Ga Boa!

00:00:28.809 --> 00:00:29.553
Get 'em!

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.991
[Rock Golems, Boss, Skeleton, and Fairy]

00:02:24.778 --> 00:02:26.611
What… What did I miss?

00:02:26.705 --> 00:02:28.896
Wait, what happened to your wounds?

00:02:29.247 --> 00:02:31.498
Oh, them? I fixed 'em up.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.586
You "fixed" them?!

00:02:32.764 --> 00:02:33.891
That easily?!

00:02:34.332 --> 00:02:39.004
Grandmother, you have my thanks for saving my men.

00:02:40.973 --> 00:02:44.984
So, you went and wrapped a fireball
around your blade, yeah?

00:02:45.412 --> 00:02:49.153
It's a clever idea, but it leaves you
vulnerable while you use it,

00:02:49.463 --> 00:02:53.588
and you run out of magic after one use.

00:02:54.058 --> 00:02:56.020
I apologize for the shameful display.

00:02:59.203 --> 00:03:00.600
Already sunset, huh?

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:04.872
You guys can take the credit for this.

00:03:04.945 --> 00:03:06.316
But Grandmother, we…

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:08.006
If not…

00:03:08.639 --> 00:03:14.002
Would you rather report that one little girl
saved the knights from certain doom?

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.979
W-What is it that you want?

00:03:17.205 --> 00:03:22.402
Just like Caerick told you,
I just want you to let me through here.

00:03:24.048 --> 00:03:24.927
I can go, right?

00:03:25.186 --> 00:03:29.502
I'll take the donkey and cart on my way back.
Take care of 'em for me, okay?

00:03:30.246 --> 00:03:32.979
Very well. Do as you please.

00:03:33.456 --> 00:03:37.019
But you will be on your own beyond here.
We can lend no aid.

00:03:37.377 --> 00:03:40.479
Sadly, that's the norm for us adventurers.

00:03:40.669 --> 00:03:43.105
Thanks for your concern, though. Later!

00:03:47.028 --> 00:03:47.829
Um…

00:03:48.466 --> 00:03:52.312
Just what is your grandmother, Captain?

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:56.002
She's probably…
the continent's most powerful adventurer.

00:03:57.741 --> 00:03:59.877
It's beyond clear after that display.

00:04:00.218 --> 00:04:03.923
If word of her existence gets out,
it would spell untold trouble.

00:04:04.372 --> 00:04:08.598
One misstep and Helshper could well be
wiped off the map.

00:04:08.837 --> 00:04:10.580
Surely that's an exaggeration…

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:11.877
Remember this.

00:04:12.191 --> 00:04:17.398
This world has monsters
that can erase a city with a single spell.

00:04:17.641 --> 00:04:19.185
O-Okay…

00:04:20.257 --> 00:04:24.103
But what exactly is Grandmother trying to do?

00:04:31.773 --> 00:04:34.935
Something about those golems' levels
doesn't sit right.

00:04:35.091 --> 00:04:35.814
Key?

00:04:35.985 --> 00:04:38.406
Eight were level 43,

00:04:38.716 --> 00:04:41.718
and one was level 172.

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:45.786
If someone was able to summon that thing,

00:04:46.211 --> 00:04:50.201
then that means there are still players
other than me, doesn't it?

00:04:50.593 --> 00:04:59.908
Per the official lore, dwarves, elves, demons,
and high elves can easily exceed 200 years of age.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:05.398
Which means it's likely the bandits' boss
is a mid-level player, huh?

00:05:05.939 --> 00:05:09.408
Level assumed to be roughly 430.

00:05:09.512 --> 00:05:11.867
Makes sense. That would be tough.

00:05:12.096 --> 00:05:16.416
Forget Caerina, even my kids
couldn't stand against that.

00:05:16.709 --> 00:05:18.485
Wonder what they're like.

00:05:18.733 --> 00:05:21.812
Well, I'm sure we'll meet 'em soon and find out.

00:05:23.704 --> 00:05:25.185
Smells great!

00:05:25.353 --> 00:05:26.420
Want some, Key?

00:05:26.786 --> 00:05:28.326
Is that a serious question?

00:05:28.805 --> 00:05:30.093
No, just a joke…

00:05:32.117 --> 00:05:33.697
So tasty!

00:05:39.487 --> 00:05:40.725
What a view!

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:43.459
So that's the Crescent-Moon Castle?

00:05:44.288 --> 00:05:46.730
And probably a Guardian Tower.

00:05:47.314 --> 00:05:48.911
Cayna, look around.

00:05:50.485 --> 00:05:52.911
Yup, looks like bandits to me.

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:55.178
Summon Magic:

00:05:55.839 --> 00:05:57.095
Brown Dragon!

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:10.875
Hey, guys. Sorry, but could I get you
to make those people behave themselves?

00:06:17.394 --> 00:06:20.002
Looks like I can leave it to them.

00:06:20.911 --> 00:06:21.915
As for me…

00:06:24.281 --> 00:06:27.098
I see you've been taking care of my men!

00:06:27.603 --> 00:06:30.240
So you're their boss, are you?

00:06:31.819 --> 00:06:35.699
[Koirogue]
Level 432, roughly as predicted.

00:06:35.699 --> 00:06:37.240
[Koirogue]
Yeah, looks like it.

00:06:37.581 --> 00:06:39.992
But I can only see his level.

00:06:40.291 --> 00:06:41.286
That armor…

00:06:41.887 --> 00:06:45.857
It's Overlord's Armor.
That nullifies the effects of magic.

00:06:46.149 --> 00:06:51.814
You've been tossing my men around
like old rags! Ain't that a bit harsh?

00:06:53.077 --> 00:06:57.711
Well, you sent rock golems
after the knights' garrison, didn't you?

00:06:57.833 --> 00:07:02.608
Oh, that was a good one.
Didn't have to get my own hands dirty.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:07.192
This may be Leadale, but it isn't
the same Leadale, you know.

00:07:08.302 --> 00:07:10.709
You tryin' to confuse me, now?

00:07:10.889 --> 00:07:15.307
The game masters are gone,
so player killers can do whatever they want!

00:07:15.533 --> 00:07:18.093
Ain't it great watchin' your level skyrocket?

00:07:18.235 --> 00:07:19.836
This is real.

00:07:20.107 --> 00:07:24.413
You can't just decide who lives and dies,
like some selfish kid!

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.802
Excuse me, this is a game!

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.538
It's my choice who I kill to raise my level!

00:07:36.579 --> 00:07:39.725
Activate all combat-oriented active skills.

00:07:40.173 --> 00:07:42.701
I'll make you see how wrong you are.

00:07:42.935 --> 00:07:44.649
This world is real!

00:07:44.932 --> 00:07:49.473
Quit spewin' nonsense.
I just told ya, it's a game!

00:07:50.994 --> 00:07:53.324
You're no match for a player.

00:07:53.411 --> 00:07:55.105
Know your place!

00:07:55.379 --> 00:07:58.389
Took the words right out of my mouth.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.677
Impossible! My Hungering Wolfblade
can't break your staff?!

00:08:06.778 --> 00:08:11.398
Sorry to break it to you, but even if
your sword has a weapon-destruction effect,

00:08:11.706 --> 00:08:15.297
it won't work against rare or extra items.

00:08:15.466 --> 00:08:16.730
You need to read up.

00:08:16.851 --> 00:08:18.565
Wait, you're a player?!

00:08:18.615 --> 00:08:23.408
Slow on the uptake, much? I've been saying
things only a player could know.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.237
Are those ears just for show?

00:08:26.242 --> 00:08:28.312
Then how about this?!

00:08:28.642 --> 00:08:30.295
Destruction Hurricane, is it?

00:08:33.673 --> 00:08:38.600
Weapon Skill, Greatsword Specialization:
Destruction Hurricane!

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:41.690
Think you can block this?

00:08:43.273 --> 00:08:46.506
Weapon Skill: Cracking Earth!

00:08:52.207 --> 00:08:58.504
Y-You bitch! What's with this hole?!
What the hell skill was that?!

00:09:00.799 --> 00:09:02.433
So you're a demon, then?

00:09:03.057 --> 00:09:05.505
You've been hiding your stats!

00:09:05.884 --> 00:09:07.714
You think it's fair to cheat?!

00:09:08.986 --> 00:09:10.294
What are you, a kid?

00:09:10.493 --> 00:09:14.698
For cryin' out loud…
Wait, maybe he really is a kid.

00:09:15.303 --> 00:09:20.072
You can't see detailed stats
for higher-level opponents.

00:09:20.399 --> 00:09:22.048
You didn't even know that?

00:09:22.326 --> 00:09:27.926
What? You sayin' a chump like you
is a higher level than…?!

00:09:29.073 --> 00:09:29.929
Ow, ow, ow!

00:09:34.698 --> 00:09:39.616
This Overlord's Armor nullifies magic!
Bet you didn't know that, jerk!

00:09:39.884 --> 00:09:41.697
Oh, I knew.

00:09:41.919 --> 00:09:46.106
It wouldn't have worked in the game,
but don't think reality's the same way!

00:09:47.077 --> 00:09:47.894
Extend!

00:09:52.883 --> 00:09:54.312
The Ruyi Jingu Bang.

00:09:54.605 --> 00:09:58.030
It weighs over eight tons.
Maybe you've heard of it?

00:09:58.472 --> 00:10:00.306
Nah, I doubt you would have.

00:10:00.897 --> 00:10:03.513
Magic Skill: Ota Laga.

00:10:06.758 --> 00:10:08.907
Magic Skill: Zan Laga!

00:10:12.066 --> 00:10:15.008
Magic Skill: Crin Ging Giga!

00:10:16.221 --> 00:10:17.755
W-Why, you…

00:10:20.003 --> 00:10:20.653
You…!

00:10:21.589 --> 00:10:24.399
Hey, that hurts! Why'd you hit me?!

00:10:24.701 --> 00:10:25.703
Yeah, it hurts.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:28.994
How have you not realized that that's real pain?

00:10:29.822 --> 00:10:32.591
I-I mean… This is a game, right?

00:10:32.692 --> 00:10:35.101
Even if we die, we can just reset, right?

00:10:35.238 --> 00:10:38.831
If you die, it's over. There are no continues.

00:10:39.186 --> 00:10:40.403
No lives left.

00:10:40.847 --> 00:10:42.320
And no reset button, either.

00:10:42.889 --> 00:10:44.009
My condolences.

00:10:44.399 --> 00:10:46.774
No way! S-Spare me!

00:10:47.011 --> 00:10:49.905
I'm still just a kid!

00:10:50.054 --> 00:10:51.196
So what?

00:10:52.193 --> 00:10:54.823
Do you know what "you reap what you sow" means?

00:10:55.212 --> 00:10:58.284
You need to take responsibility
for your own actions.

00:10:58.619 --> 00:11:03.426
Do you know how many people you
and your bandits have harmed?

00:11:03.812 --> 00:11:05.049
Do you even remember?

00:11:08.716 --> 00:11:12.302
H-Help me! Somebody help!

00:11:13.499 --> 00:11:14.417
Goodbye.

00:11:17.327 --> 00:11:19.735
Key, why didn't you warn me?!

00:11:19.913 --> 00:11:23.120
That attack would not have caused any damage.

00:11:24.873 --> 00:11:25.894
Oh, I see.

00:11:32.431 --> 00:11:34.409
They followed me, huh?

00:11:35.686 --> 00:11:39.091
I wish I could speak more smoothly.

00:11:40.889 --> 00:11:43.028
Love me down to my very bones!

00:11:47.592 --> 00:11:48.806
Good work out there.

00:11:49.254 --> 00:11:50.005
Thanks, guys.

00:11:51.537 --> 00:11:53.905
So, why'd you stop me?

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.802
I was about to finish him.

00:11:57.686 --> 00:11:59.488
He's the bandits' boss.

00:11:59.929 --> 00:12:05.311
Grandmother, could you
let us judge this criminal in Helshper?

00:12:05.648 --> 00:12:10.003
Seriously? Do you think you can keep him confined?

00:12:10.235 --> 00:12:14.191
He's more than head and shoulders above you.
You don't clear his shoes.

00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:18.845
If you say so, it must be true.

00:12:19.313 --> 00:12:20.128
Still…

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:30.225
Well, whatever. Fine.

00:12:34.611 --> 00:12:38.038
But I can't just let you take him as he is now.

00:12:41.174 --> 00:12:42.532
W-What's this?

00:12:43.349 --> 00:12:44.946
M-My stats!

00:12:45.313 --> 00:12:48.607
My stats and level are down 90%!

00:12:48.966 --> 00:12:50.395
W-What is this?!

00:12:50.591 --> 00:12:53.317
Equipment? A Discipline Collar?!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.022
W-Wait, if you had this collar, then…

00:12:57.147 --> 00:13:01.123
Y-You! You're a Limit Breaker?!

00:13:01.283 --> 00:13:04.482
You might just wish you had died here.

00:13:05.071 --> 00:13:07.379
I'm glad you learned where you stand.

00:13:08.725 --> 00:13:11.025
Grandmother, what is that collar?

00:13:11.327 --> 00:13:14.211
With this on him, you
ought to be able to handle him.

00:13:14.692 --> 00:13:17.525
But if you're careless, he can still trip you up.

00:13:18.562 --> 00:13:23.692
There's probably only one person besides me
who could take the collar off of him,

00:13:24.062 --> 00:13:29.297
but if it does come off, keep in mind
that he could easily kill all of you at once.

00:13:30.427 --> 00:13:31.386
I understand.

00:13:31.572 --> 00:13:32.409
One more thing.

00:13:32.879 --> 00:13:37.186
The collar is lowering his abilities
to one tenth their normal level,

00:13:37.418 --> 00:13:40.120
but it won't do anything to his item box.

00:13:40.385 --> 00:13:45.033
He may have items that can be used
at low levels, or even explosives,

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:49.902
so I recommend tying him up
tight enough that he can't move.

00:13:50.669 --> 00:13:54.889
I will keep that firmly in mind.
Thank you, Grandmother.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:14:01.004
I hope handing him over wasn't a bad idea…

00:14:01.592 --> 00:14:04.294
Whatever. Only a god could see the future.

00:14:04.621 --> 00:14:05.620
Now, then…

00:14:10.264 --> 00:14:11.339
Knew it.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.697
This is a Guardian Tower.

00:14:16.611 --> 00:14:22.500
Defenders against chaos,
deliver this corrupted world from its clutches!

00:14:31.957 --> 00:14:33.273
Ouch!

00:14:36.017 --> 00:14:36.924
Owww…

00:14:37.422 --> 00:14:39.714
What's the big idea…?

00:14:48.716 --> 00:14:49.739
Guess that's it?

00:14:53.384 --> 00:14:55.505
Alright, I'll give you some magic.

00:14:59.908 --> 00:15:01.341
Nothing's happening?

00:15:01.755 --> 00:15:04.796
Maybe it's the throne, instead?

00:15:09.679 --> 00:15:11.703
So that was the Guardian?

00:15:12.013 --> 00:15:15.807
First that dumb entrance, and now this…
Talk about messed up.

00:15:24.583 --> 00:15:28.096
How audacious of you,
coming somewhere this remote.

00:15:28.799 --> 00:15:31.600
I suppose I have no choice but to welcome you.

00:15:31.899 --> 00:15:33.818
Please do feel honored by it.

00:15:34.583 --> 00:15:35.168
Hey.

00:15:35.477 --> 00:15:39.822
I'm Skill Master No.03, Cayna the high elf.

00:15:40.114 --> 00:15:41.565
Whose tower is this?

00:15:41.798 --> 00:15:44.645
Oho, so you were one of Master's equals?

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:46.504
Then I shall deign to inform you.

00:15:46.976 --> 00:15:49.123
Why are you acting all superior?

00:15:49.509 --> 00:15:54.990
This tower is under the control of one
Opuskettenshultheimer Crosstettbomber.

00:15:55.254 --> 00:15:56.219
Surely you…

00:15:56.764 --> 00:15:57.373
Oh!

00:15:57.686 --> 00:16:00.298
The Mansion of Bloodlust and Malice? Really?

00:16:02.219 --> 00:16:06.559
This place is loaded with traps.
If those bandits actually got in,

00:16:06.671 --> 00:16:08.518
they'd have died, for sure.

00:16:08.938 --> 00:16:14.806
So this is Opus's tower. Now I know why the place
and its guardian are so weird…

00:16:14.897 --> 00:16:16.806
Who are you calling weird?!

00:16:17.039 --> 00:16:22.520
You won't find another skeleton
who oozes a more noble aura than mine!

00:16:22.809 --> 00:16:26.607
Really, Opus, also known as Leadale's Kongming?

00:16:28.232 --> 00:16:33.398
There's more to it, but it's largely
thanks to him that I got so strong.

00:16:33.787 --> 00:16:36.611
And he's gone, too…

00:16:36.861 --> 00:16:41.408
Ugh. Please do refrain from
sudden bouts of depression in others' towers!

00:16:41.575 --> 00:16:42.744
It's unsightly!

00:16:43.186 --> 00:16:43.828
Take this!

00:16:45.666 --> 00:16:47.390
A ring? And a book?

00:16:47.509 --> 00:16:53.022
My master left these in my care,
believing that you would one day come here.

00:16:53.147 --> 00:16:55.206
Now show some gratitude and take them.

00:16:56.684 --> 00:16:57.971
Thanks.

00:16:59.908 --> 00:17:01.303
Oh, this is…

00:17:07.307 --> 00:17:08.594
Is something the matter?

00:17:10.127 --> 00:17:11.974
How should I put this…?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.221
Why are you just holding the book open?

00:17:20.385 --> 00:17:22.201
What, only I can see her?

00:17:26.633 --> 00:17:29.113
She looks kinda familiar…

00:17:30.809 --> 00:17:32.465
Who are you?

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:36.541
I don't really get it, but if Opus gave her to me,

00:17:36.911 --> 00:17:40.006
this fairy must be here for a reason.

00:17:41.532 --> 00:17:44.201
You've finally made a fitting expression.

00:17:45.471 --> 00:17:49.665
I'd rather you not wander about
my master's tower with a sour face.

00:17:50.099 --> 00:17:51.537
Thanks, by the way.

00:17:51.856 --> 00:17:56.699
Anyway, I'm gonna get going. Let me know
if your magic points start running low again.

00:17:56.799 --> 00:17:59.494
I-If you insist, I guess I shall.

00:17:59.662 --> 00:18:02.416
I suppose you are my acting master, after all.

00:18:02.615 --> 00:18:06.306
As such, it's only natural for me
to not refuse your aid when needed.

00:18:06.566 --> 00:18:08.288
Why are you playing hard to get?

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:14.301
Well, I guess I should head back to town.

00:18:15.325 --> 00:18:20.316
I guess my next goal is figuring out
how to communicate with this fairy.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:22.183
Let's take things slow.

00:18:22.476 --> 00:18:23.307
Good idea.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:29.407
You did a great deed the other day, Grandmother.

00:18:30.132 --> 00:18:36.306
As a representative of all merchants, allow me
to thank you for dealing with the bandits.

00:18:36.722 --> 00:18:38.326
You don't have to thank me.

00:18:38.486 --> 00:18:41.675
So, what happened with that demon?

00:18:42.023 --> 00:18:43.859
As you suggested,

00:18:44.298 --> 00:18:48.903
he has been tightly bound, and is being held
in a secure underground prison.

00:18:49.425 --> 00:18:52.983
He seems to be in a stupor,
not planning any escape.

00:18:53.282 --> 00:18:57.905
Don't let your guard down. He's still a child.
You never know what he might do.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:02.796
I understand. Also, here.
Please accept your payment.

00:19:03.419 --> 00:19:08.917
This is the total reward for all the
adventurers' guild's bandit suppression requests.

00:19:09.185 --> 00:19:11.826
Naturally, we didn't provide your name.

00:19:12.385 --> 00:19:16.806
All the thankful merchants are
raising a toast to a nameless adventurer.

00:19:17.276 --> 00:19:20.586
Um, isn't this a little too much?

00:19:20.799 --> 00:19:24.500
In truth, that's how valuable
your contributions were.

00:19:25.095 --> 00:19:29.412
The state was even going to
write you a letter of thanks.

00:19:30.601 --> 00:19:32.002
I had them reconsider.

00:19:33.105 --> 00:19:37.200
I figured you didn't want to become
famous overnight, Grandmother.

00:19:37.467 --> 00:19:39.021
Thanks for that.

00:19:39.359 --> 00:19:44.900
If you went and handed me a summons to the castle,
I don't know what I'd have done!

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:50.298
Though I have informed the king, the chancellor,
and the knight-captain about you.

00:19:50.775 --> 00:19:55.282
That you are related to the
Guardian Towers, and don't care for authority.

00:19:55.821 --> 00:19:59.821
I doubt they will bother you
under most circumstances,

00:20:00.023 --> 00:20:01.902
but I wanted you to be aware.

00:20:01.953 --> 00:20:03.113
Okay, got it.

00:20:03.519 --> 00:20:07.085
That reminds me, I wanted to talk
about your flame blade move.

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:09.115
Did you invent it yourself?

00:20:09.506 --> 00:20:15.703
It embarrasses me to admit it, but some time ago
I saw an adventurer use a move like it,

00:20:16.106 --> 00:20:18.236
and used that as a reference.

00:20:18.671 --> 00:20:23.509
Of course, the adventurer
I used as reference was more powerful.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:27.713
Sounds like that adventurer
might have been a player.

00:20:28.173 --> 00:20:32.180
I think that move might have been
called Iya la Doul.

00:20:32.336 --> 00:20:37.217
It sent some crescent moon-shaped blades flying
when they swung their sword, right?

00:20:37.593 --> 00:20:42.594
That's it, exactly! If you know of it,
does that mean you can also use it, Grandmother?

00:20:43.189 --> 00:20:46.114
I am a Skill Master, after all!

00:20:46.306 --> 00:20:48.960
Could I convince you to instruct me in it?!

00:20:49.205 --> 00:20:53.304
If you want a skill scroll,
you'll need to pass a tower's trial.

00:20:53.596 --> 00:20:55.894
It's not something so easily given.

00:20:56.313 --> 00:20:58.670
Tower? Do you mean the Crescent-Moon Cas…?

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:01.310
Don't you dare set foot in there!

00:21:01.488 --> 00:21:03.369
You'd be walking to your death!

00:21:03.488 --> 00:21:05.839
Don't throw your life away!

00:21:05.853 --> 00:21:08.323
I understand. I'll keep clear.

00:21:08.597 --> 00:21:11.499
I'll find another tower's trial to challenge.

00:21:12.009 --> 00:21:12.684
Good.

00:21:12.868 --> 00:21:13.943
Grandmother…

00:21:14.678 --> 00:21:18.778
I'm told our current business
with Elineh is nearly done.

00:21:19.087 --> 00:21:21.913
Will you be returning to Felskeilo?

00:21:22.232 --> 00:21:23.811
If he's going, I am.

00:21:24.002 --> 00:21:25.516
I'll miss having you here.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:29.696
Well, if you need me
for something other than combat,

00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:31.696
you can reach me through Mai-Mai.

00:21:32.055 --> 00:21:34.640
You'd come all the way here from Felskeilo?!

00:21:34.913 --> 00:21:38.242
We wouldn't want to burden you
with such a long trip!

00:21:38.486 --> 00:21:43.915
Oh, no worries there. I registered
the teleportation destination, so it'd be instant.

00:21:43.968 --> 00:21:45.272
T-Teleportation?!

00:21:45.696 --> 00:21:49.304
Oh, right! There's a lot of fun
waiting for me in Felskeilo!

00:21:49.506 --> 00:21:50.416
Fun?

00:21:50.573 --> 00:21:51.445
You mean…

00:21:51.637 --> 00:21:54.507
I had you send Mai-Mai a message, right, Caerick?

00:21:55.669 --> 00:22:00.405
I just can't wait to see the face
Mai-Mai makes when she sees me.
